# Optional overrides for local development.
#
# You do not need this file to run Orbit. `make setup` generates a .env with the
# machine-local secrets, and every other value has a default: compose settings in
# docker-compose.yml, and in-cluster settings in deploy/local/orbit-values.yaml.
#
# Copy a line into .env only when you need to change it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bedrock (optional). Enables Bedrock providers in the inference gateway.
# Set BEDROCK_ACCOUNTS to a comma-separated list of aliases. Each alias
# becomes a distinct provider "bedrock:<alias>" in the model catalog.
#
# AWS_PROFILE selects your named AWS SSO profile. `make up` and
# `make cluster-bedrock-creds` export credentials from it automatically —
# BEDROCK_<ALIAS>_ACCESS_KEY_ID, BEDROCK_<ALIAS>_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, and
# BEDROCK_<ALIAS>_SESSION_TOKEN are derived from your SSO session and written
# directly into the cluster secret; you do not set them here.
#
# For each alias, set BEDROCK_<ALIAS>_REGION to the AWS region.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BEDROCK_ACCOUNTS=aus,us
# AWS_PROFILE=your-sso-profile
#
# BEDROCK_AUS_REGION=ap-southeast-2
# BEDROCK_US_REGION=us-west-2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backing services. Defaults live in docker-compose.yml. Override only if the
# ports collide with something else on your machine.
#
# Changing DB_PASSWORD after the first `make up` will not work: Postgres bakes
# the password into its volume at first initialisation. Run `make dev-down-clean`
# to drop the volume first.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DB_PORT=5432
# DB_USER=orbit
# DB_NAME=orbit
# DB_PASSWORD=orbit
# REDIS_PORT=6379
# REDIS_PASSWORD=orbit

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tenant used by `make auth`. Defaults to `example`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ORBIT_TENANT_ID=example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Parallel image builds (optional, high-spec machines only).
#
# By default `make redeploy-platform` (and therefore `make up` /
# `make redeploy`) builds each image serially — safe on any machine. Setting
# this flag builds all platform images in one parallel `docker buildx bake`
# graph instead, which dedups the shared Go module and source layers across
# images and is much faster on hardware with headroom.
#
# Only enable it when your Docker VM has at least ~12 CPUs / 24 GiB; give it
# more if the host allows (e.g. `colima start --cpu 12 --memory 32`). On
# smaller VMs the concurrent build pressure cascades into mesh and Postgres
# failures — leave it unset there.
# See docs/adr/2026-07-21-ci-pipeline-and-local-build-parallelisation.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ORBIT_PARALLEL_BUILDS=1
